# =========================================================================
# 2D Montessori — root .gitignore
# Covers Dart/Flutter workspace, Firebase tooling, Cloud Functions (Node/TS),
# environment/config, and OS/editor noise. See docs/architecture/environments.md
# for how real values are supplied at build/deploy time.
# =========================================================================

# ---- OS / editor / local tooling ----
.claude/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp

# ---- Dart / Flutter (applies under apps/*, packages/*) ----
**/.dart_tool/
**/.packages
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/build/
**/.pub-cache/
**/.pub/
**/pubspec.lock
!/pubspec.lock
**/*.g.dart
**/*.freezed.dart
**/*.mocks.dart
**/coverage/
**/.symlinks/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
**/android/.gradle/
**/android/local.properties
**/*.iml

# Web build output
**/web/build/

# ---- Environment / secrets (never commit real values) ----
# Real per-environment values live outside git or in a secrets manager.
# Only *.example.json files are tracked; see config/env/README.md.
config/env/*.json
!config/env/*.example.json
*.env
.env*
!.env.example

# ---- Firebase ----
# Generated FlutterFire options contain per-project (non-secret but
# project-specific) identifiers. Only the .template files are tracked
# until a given environment's real project exists — see
# docs/architecture/environments.md. staging/prod stay excluded (those
# projects don't exist yet, so there's nothing real to commit); dev's two
# generated files are explicitly un-ignored below now that
# twod-montessori-dev is real and confirmed, and CI needs them to compile
# main_dev.dart at all (it always does a fresh checkout, so a gitignored
# file can never "already exist" there the way it can locally). Firebase
# Web config is not a credential — the security boundary is Firestore/
# Storage Rules and App Check, not hiding this file; see
# docs/architecture/decisions.md's Dev deployment-prep section.
**/lib/firebase_options*.dart
!**/lib/firebase_options*.dart.template
!apps/public_web/lib/firebase_options_dev.dart
!apps/admin_web/lib/firebase_options_dev.dart
# FlutterFire CLI's own per-app bookkeeping file (which options file maps
# to which Firebase Web App id) — same generated-artifact policy as
# firebase_options*.dart above, not the root /firebase.json (that one,
# the actual Hosting/deploy config, IS tracked).
apps/*/firebase.json
.firebaserc
!.firebaserc.template
# Firebase CLI's local per-machine deploy cache (e.g. Hosting's
# incremental-upload file-hash cache) — created by real `firebase
# deploy` runs, never meant to be committed.
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firebase-export-*/
ui-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
pubsub-debug.log
database-debug.log
storage-debug.log
*.emulator-data/

# Service account keys / admin credentials — must never be committed.
**/*serviceAccount*.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json

# ---- Cloud Functions (Node/TypeScript) ----
functions/node_modules/
functions/lib/
functions/*.log
functions/.env
functions/.env.*
!functions/.env.example

# ---- Any other Node-based tooling (e.g. firebase/test/) ----
**/node_modules/

# ---- CI / misc ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
